<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bugis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Buginese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bugis are a people of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, known for their seafaring and trade and for their epic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-galigo">La Galigo</a>, written in their own Lontara script. Their kingdoms included Bone, Wajo and Soppeng. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makassar-war">Makassar War</a> of 1666–1669 many Bugis migrated across the archipelago as traders and warriors; in Johor-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riau">Riau</a> they held the office of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> from 1722, and they founded the sultanate of Selangor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bugis.jpg" alt="Bugis" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rejalobo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IMG-20190222-WA0014.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
